# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# Persistent simulations on a GPU (D196), scenario nvt of
# Inputs/python_segments.py.
# NVT runs (velocity Verlet and leapfrog, in double and mixed precision) of
# 1 + 7 + 13 steps, and of 1 x 5 + 3 x 2 + 10, against uninterrupted ones,
# equal to the bit (D215), and the phase of the coupling
# across their boundaries.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_segments.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU mdir %t nvt | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: NVT VelocityVerlet Double: parts of 1+7+13 and of 1x5+3x2+10 equal 21 steps in one part to the bit
# CHECK: NVT VelocityVerlet Mixed: parts of 1+7+13 and of 1x5+3x2+10 equal 21 steps in one part to the bit
# CHECK: NVT: the coupling moves the velocities
# CHECK: NVT Leapfrog Double: parts of 1+7+13 and of 1x5+3x2+10 equal 21 steps in one part to the bit
# CHECK: NVT Leapfrog Mixed: parts of 1+7+13 and of 1x5+3x2+10 equal 21 steps in one part to the bit
# CHECK: segments nvt passed
